page('/en/electricity-price-today/', { app: true, title: 'Electricity Price Netherlands Today (Hourly & 15-min) | Stroomprijs', desc: `Today’s dynamic electricity price in the Netherlands per hour (${enDate(TODAY)}): price class A–G, the cheapest and most expensive hour, the cheapest block and an estimate incl. tax. Market price excl. VAT.`, modified: LIVE_UPDATED, schema: graph(crumbs(['Electricity price today', '/en/electricity-price-today/']), dayDataset('/en/electricity-price-today/', TODAY, true)), body: `<header class="pg-h"><h1>Electricity price today</h1><p>${enDate(TODAY)}</p></header>${staleEn}${modebar(false, true)}${daySec('today', 'Price per hour', true)}${planner('today', true)}<div class="prose"><p>The prices come from the EPEX Spot day-ahead auction for the Dutch bidding zone. That auction takes place the day before, around 12:00 ${tzNow}; the result is also published on the ENTSO-E Transparency Platform. Since 1 October 2025 the day-ahead market sets a price per quarter-hour; this page shows the hourly prices that EnergyZero publishes. Some suppliers bill per quarter-hour, so check your contract. See also <a href="${BASE}/en/electricity-price-tomorrow/">tomorrow’s electricity price</a> and <a href="${BASE}/en/guides/dynamic-electricity-price-how-it-works/">how dynamic prices work</a>.</p></div>${placeholderEn}${updatedEn}` });
